---
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { GA4_ID, LEGAL } from '../../data/site-config';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Legal notices for this Irish salary calculator 2026" description="Publisher details, editorial responsibility, terms of use and the disclaimer applying to every figure this calculator produces, plus how to raise a complaint.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 pt-4 pb-8 prose prose-slate">
    <h1>Legal Notice</h1>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <p>irishnetpay.com is an independent salary calculator. It is not affiliated with Revenue, the Department of Finance, or any government body. It is published by:</p>
    <LegalIdentity mode="publisher" lang="en" />

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <LegalIdentity mode="hosting" lang="en" />

    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <p>If you believe your personal data has been mishandled, you may complain to {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}, whose contact details are at <a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>.</p>
    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>Results are estimates based on 2026 tax rates and thresholds. They do not constitute tax advice. Consult Revenue.ie or a qualified tax advisor for your specific situation.</p>
    <h2>Personal data and cookies</h2>
    <p>The calculators keep nothing: the salary and credits you enter are processed in your browser and disappear when you close the tab. The site sets Google Analytics audience measurement cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_{GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code>, 13 months at most), with no advertising; page stability is monitored with Microsoft Clarity, cookieless and with content masked. Details, legal basis and how to object: our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and its <a href="/privacy/#cookies">cookies</a> section.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
